# AddressSanitizer suppressions (same story as valgrind.supp).
#
# KNOWN KERNEL ARTIFACT (libcorm, not libsepal):
# the kernel keeps the *borrowed* filename pointer passed to corm_open() and
# its exit-time destructor (corm_destruct -> corm_close -> corm_get ->
# corm_id_ex -> strlen) dereferences it after the caller's frame returned
# (stack-use-after-return on the consumer's path buffer). In practice the
# stale stack bytes still hold the path at exit, so this is benign outside
# sanitizers — but it is a genuine kernel ownership bug, also exercised by
# mm's own reopen flows. Fixing it belongs to a kernel quest, not R5a.
interceptor_via_fun:corm_destruct
